edit /etc/securettys and add the device you are going to be using to 
gain root access

        /dev/console
        local:0
        :0
        /dev/tty00
        ptys

Add yourself to the /etc/group file.  I'm not sure which you really 
need, but here is what I add:

        system:*:0:root,myusernamegoeshere
        mem:*:3:root,myusernamegoeshere

Of course now just about any terminal can get root access, if they know 
the root password :-)

                                        Bob Harris


