dub@latnet.lv (Dub) wrote in message news:<6445524b.0203251238.73ee489@posting.google.com>...
> Hi,
> 
> I'm not sure how to set the exact moment of enabling/disabling
> daylight settings.
> 
> man page for tzfile(4) tells that component 'time' of environment
> variable TZ
> 'Describes the time when, __in current time__, the change to or return
> from      alternative time occurs'.
> 
> Let's take a definition from time zone source file
> /etc/zoneinfo/sources/europe
> 
> Rule    E-Eur   1981    max     -       Mar     lastSun  3:00s  1:00  
>  " DST"
> Does it mean that local time at 2:59:59 EET will jump to 4:00:00 EET
> DST?
> 
> Rule    E-Eur   1996    max     -       Oct     lastSun  3:00s  0     
>  -
> Does it mean that local time at 3:59:59 EET DST will jump to 3:00:00
> EET?
> 
> 
> Many thanks in advance for your comments! 
> 
> BR, 
> Dub

You are correct.  The "s" suffix in "3:00s" means use standard time, i.e.,
change at 0300 local standard time. If you use the "w" suffix, or no
suffix, it means use "wall clock" time, i.e., current local time.

The man page for zic(8) is a little more informative than the one for
tzfile(4).

Martin


