While I'll grant that Tru64 clustering is useful in HPTC, I question whether
it is all that much of an advantage over conventional Beowulf configurations
using already-existing third-party software and suspect that in many case it
kind of gets dragged along by the use of Alpha.  By contrast, its
high-availability features are *critical* to a commercial market that dwarfs
HPTC in size and has much less in the way of alternatives to choose from,
which is why I referred to the latter as a niche - and to Compaq's
leadership as morons.

