>
> The compiler works well, but the binary code made a lot of damage in
> the memory.
>
> I am asking if tru64 support the long long int type?

It does, but you don't need it: this is a 64 bit system, and
``long int'' has already 64 bits. ``long long int'' is just a
synonym. So,

  sprintf(buf, "%ld", st_size);

should work.

> I didn't also find the cc compiler option "FILE_OFFSET_BITS" (like in
> 7.2 RH Linux).
>

Dito: I believe that in Linux, FILE_OFFSET_BITS selects whether you
want to use 32 or 64 bit integers for file sizes/offsets. In Tru64,
you will get 64, which is what you want (files > 2GB), you don't need
to define FILE_OFFSET_BITS, as far as system libraries/headers are
concerned. However, if it is needed anywhere in your code, adding
-DFILE_OFFSET_BITS=64 to the compiler options is probably safe.

Timo


