This is less than ideal advice since it doesn't address the fact that
the new copy of the operating system remebers that its root file system
was on the source disk used for the copy.  This is likely to be a common
problem for any of the techniques that were used under V4 and earlier to
make copies of a system disk.

There is apparently a way to change the hardware database so that
this detail of the previous configuration is forgotten, allowing
the new disk to become the system disk.  The technique may have
been written up as a "Best Practices" document.  If so it will be
on the corporate web site somewhere.  The question frequently
comes up in the tru64-unix-managers mailing list, so the archives
of the mailing list may have something.  I don't have the URL for
the archives though.

