Start by booting from the install CD. Take the option to
get to the Unix Shell.
Try to mount the device and see what you can see.
If the data you want is there back it up to tape or
another drive.
If there is no data get out the backup tapes.
After this it's a question of whether you want to
use the disk (ie you think human error caused the
damage) or you don't (ie you think the hardware is
failing).
Get back to us when you have a good backup and tell us
which way you want to proceed or if you can't we can
talk you through examining the disk to see what broke
it.
Adam
PS Are you sure that the disk with the data on is dka0?
try show dev and post the output.






