How about "it might be there and it probably won't work"?

As to where the library is, it depends on the version of tru64--in
tru64 v5.0, it should be there. For v4.0, the optional CMPDEVENH
subset installs /usr/opt/alt/usr/lib/threads/libpthread.a, so they
need that subset installed, and an appropriate -L to the linker.

However, this probably won't do what you want--kernel threads are
generally very closely tied to the private kernel interfaces that
support them (one of the caveats about using a static libpthread.a is
that new versions of tru64 or even patch kits may break the
executable).  I would be *very* surprised if the Tru64 emulation in
Linux supports the tru64 kernel thread interfaces, so the resulting
executable probably won't run on Alpha Linux (if it actually is
multi-threaded--if it isn't, they should be able to link without
the pthread library).

A google search for "Butenhof libthread.a tru64" will turn up more
information on threads on tru64, but probably won't give you any help
getting such an executable to run on Alpha Linux.

