I usually modify /etc/gettydefs to do this.  Right after the comments
section and just before the entry for console, try inserting this
line:

default# B9600 # B9600 #\r\n\r\nPLEASE STAY OFF THIS SYSTEM\r\n\r\n#

I just tried this on a T5.1C system and a V5.0 system and it worked
fine in both cases.  Usual cautions apply: make sure you've got
another root login already active in case you can't log in after the
change, make a copy of the file first, and so on....

