Depending on your system type decevent or compaq analyze is used to read the
/var/adm/binary.errlog file.
compaq analyze is used on DS10, DS20, ES40, ES45, GS80/160/320 systems. You
can use decevent on these systems
but if you want to analyze a CPU related error decevent may not know how to
decipher it.

You can check to see if decevent is installed by:
setld -i |  grep -i dia

You can check if compaq analyze is installed by looking to see if WEBES is
installed. WEBES is a suite of 3 tools compaq analyze, rcm and ccat.
setld -i | grep -i webes

Dave

