On 12 Mar 2002, Peter da Silva wrote:

> In article <a6557b$18v08$1@sinclair.be.wanadoo.com>,
> Miguel Demaerel <Miguel.Demaerel@SLB.COM> wrote:
> > I need a overview of the difference between AIX, Solaris and HP and Tru64.
> 
> AIX is UNIX running hosted on an OS/360-inspired applcation layer.
> 
