On Tue, 12 Mar 2002 16:24:31 +0100, strsha <nebojsam@eunet.yu> wrote:
>I think that is not possible to have two different operating systems on the
>same hard disk.

There are at least some conditions under which it is possible to
have two operating systems on the same disk.  As long as they use
the same partition table type and don't have any other serious
conflicts, it should be possible.  I keep two entirely separate
(Redhat) Linux installations on each of my two disks--well three
installations in total.  When upgrading, I upgrade one of the
independent installations as a test, then upgrade the production
installation, then after a few weeks upgrade the third
installation.  During that interval, I have different OS versions
on the same disk and can boot either one.

Good luck, YMMV, etc.

Robert Riches
