manufacturing side.  They bought DEC for the services side.  Period, end 
of story.  (I say this with conviction because I applied to and was 
offered a job at DEC doing OpenVMS administration a few months before 
they sold out to COMPAQ and that is what the hiring manager told me 
COMPAQ was buying them for)  That is the same side that HP covets.  HP's 
PC business is for shit.  The combined firm will have #1 PCs, #2 (or #3, 
I don't exactly recall off the top of my head) services and killer 
printers/imaging (the crown jewel of HP).  HP gets economies of scale in 
commodity PCs as well as the very lucrative services division.  COMPAQ 
gets shielded (somewhat) from the low margin, commodity PC business. 
